I didn&#x27;t want to shell out for Max again, so I piped the SVG created by Max back into Fable 5.1 at its default thinking level (of high):<p><pre><code>  llm logs -cx | llm -m claude-fable-5.1 -s &#x27;animate this&#x27;
</code></pre>
Here&#x27;s the result, which cost $1.37: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;tools.simonwillison.net&#x2F;markdown-svg-renderer?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgist.github.com%2Fsimonw%2F87282467acb3652e0f99c85155554a32#response" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;tools.simonwillison.net&#x2F;markdown-svg-renderer?url=ht...</a><p>It&#x27;s excellent!
